---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AuthorBox from '../../components/AuthorBox.astro';
import Byline from '../../components/Byline.astro';
import { articleSchema, guideDates } from '../../lib/editorial';

const dates = guideDates["first-business-license"];
const description = "Who typically needs a first business license, and which desk takes the filing.";
const jsonLd = articleSchema({
  headline: "Getting Your First Business License",
  description,
  url: new URL(Astro.url.pathname, "https://licensingmadesimple.com").href,
  datePublished: dates.published,
  dateModified: dates.modified,
});
---

<Layout title="Getting Your First Business License — LicensingMadeSimple" description={description} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Getting Your First Business License</h1>
      <p>What you need, and where to file it.</p>
      <Byline published={dates.published} modified={dates.modified} />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container article" style="max-width: 720px;">
      <h2>Do you need one?</h2>
      <p>Most cities and counties require a general business license to operate. Some industries also need a state license. Financial services, healthcare, construction, and food service almost always have a state desk on top of the local one. Operating without a required license can mean fines, a cease-and-desist, or unenforceable contracts.</p>

      <h2>What kind, and where to file</h2>
      <p>Start with the city or county where the business sits. That office issues the general business license or tells you it is a county filing. Then check the state agency for your industry:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Collection / ARM: collection board, banking department, or secretary of state; some states issue no license. See the <a href="/directory/collection">collection directory</a> and the <a href="/states/arkansas/collection">Arkansas collection agency license</a>.</li>
        <li>Consumer or commercial lending — banking, DFI, or consumer-credit agency, usually on NMLS. See the <a href="/directory/lending">lending directory</a>.</li>
        <li>Money transmission — FinCEN MSB registration plus a state money-transmitter license on NMLS. See the <a href="/directory/money-transmitters">money-transmitter directory</a>.</li>
        <li>Mortgage — state mortgage regulator through NMLS. See the <a href="/directory/mortgage">mortgage directory</a>.</li>
        <li>Contractors — state contractor board and/or the city or county. See the <a href="/directory/contractors">contractor overview</a>.</li>
        <li>Insurance producers and adjusters — state department of insurance, usually through NIPR. See the <a href="/directory/insurance">insurance overview</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Not sure which vertical you are in? Use the <a href="/#wizard">roadmap wizard</a>, then open the matching state page.</p>

      <h2>What the agency usually asks for</h2>
      <p>A complete filing typically includes the application form, formation documents, control-person or owner disclosures, and, for many financial licenses, a surety bond and a registered agent. Money-transmitter applications also need a BSA/AML program and FinCEN registration. Open the state license page for any fee, bond, or timeline this directory has verified. If a cell says Varies, see regulator, open the agency link.</p>

      <h2>How long it takes</h2>
      <p>A state license page shows a timeline only when a regulator or NMLS source states one. The agency review clock, and any deficiency letter, decides the calendar. For clocks this directory has not verified, use <a href="https://fastlicence.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fastlicence.com</a>. For cited fee lines and filing paths, use <a href="https://licensestore.com/costs/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LicenseStore costs</a> and <a href="https://licensestore.com/compare/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LicenseStore compare</a>.</p>

      <h2>DIY or a filer</h2>
      <p>You can file yourself. The agency will accept a complete application from the applicant. If you want the package assembled and submitted, <a href="https://cornerstonelicensing.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cornerstone Licensing</a> does that work. We do not reprint approval-rate or speed claims here.</p>

      <p>Next: <a href="/#wizard">roadmap wizard</a> or the <a href="/states">state index</a>.</p>
      <AuthorBox />
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .article h2 { font-size: 1.2rem; margin-top: 32px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .article h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .article p, .article li { font-size: 0.93rem; color: var(--text-secondary); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .article ul { margin: 0 0 14px 20px; }
</style>
